Interviewer: "Design a distributed rate limiter backed by Redis, used to protect your API platform."

This is a great follow-up to the wallet problem because it flips the correctness concern on its head. In the wallet, a race condition costs someone money. Here, a race condition means a client sneaks past their limit — annoying, not catastrophic — but the engineering pattern to fix it (atomic operations under concurrency) is the exact same muscle. Let's build it properly.

